     "body": "I would like to take this issue and open a PR for the three ADRs.\nThe PR restates the ADR-0006 model and adds no new decision.\nI have one question about Tier A.\nADR-0007 says that a Tier A connection attaches only the project catalogs the user may read.\nThe read runs in the tool's process with no API hop.\nADR-0006 says that in a shared tenant catalog the grant is schema-scoped and the separation between projects of one tenant is application-enforced.\nADR-0008 says that direct reads enforce only at catalog/table and storage-prefix level.\nADR-0009 leaves the read engine mechanism open.\nWhat enforces the schema scope on a Tier A read in a shared catalog?\nIf this is not decided, the PR uses the ADR-0006 wording in ADR-0007 and names no mechanism.\n",
