     "body": "Hi @tieskeklump, it isn't decided yet. Today a Tier A read uses the app's own credentials, which are the same for every user. Zitadel only decides who can reach a service. The ADRs describe per-user credentials (ADR-0008, ADR-0009), but those aren't built yet, and even then they could at best be limited to a whole catalog or storage folder.\nHow tenants and users get access to data and compute is still open. We'll probably start simple, with read and write access on specific catalogs and tables.\nThe ADRs will be updated by the core maintainers, because we are currently evaluating the architecture and platform direction. These ADRs were written quite early in the design process, so they still contain gaps and contradictions like the one you found.",
